1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:09,913
This is Rasta, a night-time route checker for Delhi NCR. Most maps show you the fastest way home. Rasta shows you which way has people around.

2
00:00:10,613 --> 00:00:21,707
Pick where you're going, walking or a cab, and when you're leaving. Rasta finds up to three different routes, and scores each one for the hour you'll actually be on it.

3
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:33,426
It checks what's open along the way: shops, chemists, petrol pumps and hospitals. Hollow pins will be closed when you pass. Red dashes are stretches with nothing open.

4
00:00:34,126 --> 00:00:42,044
The score also weighs the type of road, NASA's satellite night light, CCTV mapped in OpenStreetMap, and how close help is.

5
00:00:42,747 --> 00:00:47,872
This chart shows how the route changes through the evening, so you can pick the best time to leave.

6
00:00:48,578 --> 00:00:56,365
On foot, Rasta can also suggest walking plus metro, and reminds you to check the last train late at night.

7
00:00:57,071 --> 00:01:06,335
Save your trusted contacts once. Then one tap gets a message ready for all of them, with your route, arrival time and current location.

8
00:01:07,035 --> 00:01:11,538
And a two-tap question after each search helps tune the score with real answers.

9
00:01:14,938 --> 00:01:17,892
Prefer it bright? There's a light mode too.

10
00:01:19,669 --> 00:01:27,516
Built only on open data. It doesn't promise safety. It helps you choose. Rasta. For the ride home.

